   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pakistan Floods Emergency Appeal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Floods in Pakistan have affected some 33 million people and killed at least 1,314, including 458 children, Pakistan&apos;s National Disaster Management Agency said.   Estimates suggest the floods have caused at least $10bn (8.5bn) of damage. One-third of Pakistan is now underwater. Unprecedented monsoon rains- the terrifying consequences of climate change- have caused devastating floods, affecting a staggering 33 MILLION PEOPLE (1 in 7 Pakistanis) and killing over 2,000 people so far.</narrative>
  </description>
